  "salt": "oeNRfu6RCHLSuYiruyns6Q==",
  "text": "Dechtire, also written Dechtere, Deichtine, or Dectora, was an Irish heroine or goddess. She was the mother of the hero Cúchulainn. She lived at Emain Macha, the capital of Ulster, with her brother or father, king Concobar mac Nessa. She and her fifty maidens vanished one day without trace. Years later a flock of fifty-one birds appeared around the capital and ate every blade of grass until the fields were barren. The warriors of Ulster hunted the birds in chariots. The birds flew in pairs joined by silver chains, led by one wearing a silver yoke. The hunt ended at a distant house where a wondrous child was found. Dechtire conceived the boy by swallowing a worm from a glass of wine, or by the god Lugh. The boy was later called Sétanta. She gave birth and remained a virgin. Ulster's greatest heroes agreed to share the boy's upbringing.",
